Original commit body from 4a910c2:

Repos with many entrypoints (e.g., redis with 158 main() functions)
previously produced 0 edges in compact mode because all max_symbols
slots were consumed by force-included entrypoints, leaving no room
for the connectivity-aware algorithm to add bridge nodes.

Now entrypoints are capped to max_symbols // 2 (minimum 1), keeping
the highest-confidence entries. The remaining budget is used by
connectivity-aware selection to add nodes that connect the subgraph.

Before: redis compact → 158 nodes, 0 edges
After:  redis compact → 100 nodes, 175 edges
